# Auth

The library sends a bearer access token on every resource call. It does not create, refresh, or revoke tokens.

## Public construction

```php
use AleBatistella\BlingErpApi\Bling;

$bling = new Bling($accessToken);
```

`Bling::__construct(string $accessToken)` asks `IoC::getRepository` for the repository and keeps it on the client (`src/Bling.php`).

## What IoC wires

`src/Providers/IoC.php`:

| Piece | Value |
|-------|--------|
| Base URL | `https://www.bling.com.br/Api/v3/` |
| Header | `Authorization: Bearer {accessToken}` |
| Client | `BlingRepository` |

The token and base URL stay fixed for that `Bling` instance. Resource methods do not accept a token argument.

## Where the token comes from

The caller already holds an access token from Bling's `/oauth/token` endpoint. Document that boundary with:

- `README.md` — `new Bling($apiKey)` and the link to token issuance
- `https://developer.bling.com.br/aplicativos#tokens-de-acesso`
- `demo/` — Laravel sample that posts the authorization code to `https://www.bling.com.br/Api/v3/oauth/token` and then constructs `new Bling($accessToken)`

## Tests

Facade tests call `new Bling(fake()->word())`. Do not request a real token and do not call live Bling.
